            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>The vertex is $$\left( {0,0} \right).$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since the vertex is $$\left( {0,0} \right),$$ both the x- and y-intercepts are the point $$\left( {0,0} \right).$$ To graph the parabola we need more points. In this case it is easiest to choose values of y.</p>
        <p>We also plot the points symmetric to $$\left( {2,1} \right)$$ and $$\left( {8,2} \right)$$ across the y-axis, the points $$\left( {2,-1} \right),$$$$\left( {8,-2} \right).$$</p>
        <p>Graph the parabola.</p>
      </solution>
